572 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 366 0 R
/E (In software engineering, a Data Flow Diagram \(DFD\) is a graphical tool that visualizes how data moves through a system, showing its inputs, outputs, processes, and storage points. DFDs help system analysts and stakeholders understand complex systems by illustrating the flow of information between external entities and internal processes. They consist of four main components: external entities \(data sources/sinks\), processes \(data transformations\), data stores \(where data is held\), and data flows \(paths data travels\).)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
